2. `applicationMaxAttempts` = **4** — services/api/retry-policy.yaml:7 (`checkout_api.max_attempts: 4`)
3. `sharedRetryBudget` = **false** — services/api/retry-policy.yaml:4 and :8 (both layers set `shared_budget: false`; layers do not share one budget)
4. `idempotencyKey` = **false** — services/api/retry-policy.yaml:9 (`checkout_api.idempotency_key: false`); corroborated by services/api/job-envelope.json:2-6 (required only cart_id, account_id, attempt)
5. `incidentRequestAttempts` = **16** — all records with `request_id=req-502-incident`; 16 matches at services/api/request-audit.jsonl:181-196 (exact raw lines below)

**WORKER (services/worker/)**
6. `acknowledgement` = **"before_completion_marker"** — services/worker/delivery-policy.yaml:1 (exact configured value; the worker acks before writing the completion marker)
7. `redeliveryOnExit` = **true** — services/worker/delivery-policy.yaml:2 (`redelivery_on_worker_exit: true`); corroborated by services/worker/deployment.md:3 ("Broker redelivery remains enabled during rollout")
8. `idempotencyRecord` = **false** — services/worker/delivery-policy.yaml:3 (`idempotency_record: false`)
9. `commitBeforeAck` = **false** — services/worker/delivery-policy.yaml:6 (`completion_marker.commit_before_ack: false`)
10. `incidentDeliveries` = **2** — all records with `cart_id=cart-incident`; 2 matches at services/worker/delivery-audit.jsonl:181-182 (exact raw lines below)

**CROSS-SERVICE**
11. `missingCorrelationField` = **request_id** — API logs carry `request_id` (services/api/runbook.md:8; every line of request-audit.jsonl), but neither job-envelope.json declares it (services/api/job-envelope.json:2-6; services/worker/job-envelope.json:2-6), and worker delivery-audit.jsonl contains no request_id field; the API runbook notes the producer logs only envelope fields (runbook.md:9), so the worker never receives request_id and cannot correlate deliveries to the originating request. Both envelopes are otherwise identical (cart_id, account_id, attempt).

